    "result_text": "Done. The build passes.\n\nI extended `BusinessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay` to skip public holidays in addition to weekends. Key changes:\n\n- Added the fixed public-holiday set (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28) as a constant.\n- Replaced the single weekend-to-Monday jump with a loop that rolls forward one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed holiday \u2014 so a date landing on a holiday (or a holiday adjacent to a weekend, like the 12-25/12-28 cluster) correctly advances to the next non-holiday business day.\n- Extracted the check into a small private `isNonBusinessDay` helper to keep the method's single responsibility clear.\n\nThe logic stayed in the existing `BusinessDayAdjuster`, which is the sole place both call sites (`Owner` and `OwnerRestControllerV1`) already delegate to, so no logic was duplicated. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
